{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "id": "msg_011Ch1rc79pqNERZTybgLy9Z", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "I've stopped testing because the device connection failed and I could not finish the sweep. I did not sign off.\n\n**Device state:** Every device call since the rotate to landscape has returned `BrokenPipeError`, including observe, screenshot, wait and open_app. The app was last seen on the group editor in portrait. The Plan group-card tap and the rotate may not have run, so the device could be on any screen.\n\n**Reports filed: 1 (developer could not reproduce).** The first report was a night-owl preview issue: with night owl on, today's 8:30 PM dose appeared to vanish from the preview. The clock read 12:09 AM, and night owl treats times before 04:00 as the previous day, so the preview was consistent. That report was a misreading on my part.\n\nI also filed a Home vs Plan \"Nothing scheduled today\" mismatch, which the developer could not reproduce either. It happened under the same 00:xx night-owl condition. With night owl off, Home and Plan agreed, so I consider that report invalid too.\n\n**Checked and passing:**\n- **Group first-dose picker (changed item):** OK kept the stored value, Cancel discarded changes, a minute-only change applied (9:08 → 9:30 AM), a PM-only change applied (9:30 AM → 9:30 PM), and 12:08 AM applied. Discard on the editor restored the saved value.\n- **Medicine category headers (changed item):** headers appear only for categories with medicines. Adding Antiandrogen created its header; archiving its only medicine removed it; renaming Estradiol kept its header.\n- **Journal entry cache (changed item):** a new note, an edited note, a cancelled edit, and a deleted note all persisted correctly across tab switches, including a Plan → Journal route. The Start HRT timeline date showed and was pinned on Home.\n- **Group setup and schedule:** Weekly with an interval of 2 weeks and Mon/Sat days gave a correct preview and Plan/Home entries. Zero days disabled Save, and an empty name disabled Save. A group rename persisted. A new group's default name was \"Group 2\", and Cancel created nothing. Adding Estradiol twice as Oral and Sublingual gave two correct entries on Plan and Home.\n- **Rotation:** the journal survived landscape and portrait with no data loss.\n\n**Not done:** the night-owl caption in landscape (the \"cut-off text\" change), and any check after the device drops. Plan and Home for dates beyond Nov 16 were not checked.\n\nOnce the device is reachable, the first step is to re-observe, then rotate the group editor to landscape and check the night-owl caption for truncation. If the device stays down, I can't verify those areas and the sweep is incomplete."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 205, "cache_read_input_tokens": 262938, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 205}, "output_tokens": 5, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "0c751574-2f6e-4d4f-af98-6c2b6d43dcec", "uuid": "391d4a53-e138-4b8d-936e-618cf88b2c6d", "timestamp": "2026-11-14T00:14:58.908Z", "request_id": "req_011Ch1rc6sxynpEfyEPxuQRW"}
